---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Sanskar Pandey. Backend, systems, and AI engineer; notes, and things built from scratch.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article style="max-width: 46rem;">
      <section class="hero" style="padding-block: 3.5rem 1rem;">
        <p class="label hero__eyebrow rise rise-1">About</p>
        <h1 class="rise rise-2">Hi, I&rsquo;m Sanskar.</h1>
      </section>

      <div class="prose rise rise-3" style="max-width: 42rem;">
        <p class="big-lede">
          I work the hard middle of the stack: storage engines, backend and API
          infrastructure, LLM and agent systems, and the reliability work that decides
          whether any of it survives production.
        </p>

        <p>
          Most of what is on this site I built from scratch to actually understand it,
          not to ship:
          <a href="https://github.com/sanskarpan/btree-engine">B+Tree</a> and
          <a href="https://github.com/sanskarpan/lsm-tree-storage">LSM-tree</a> storage
          engines, a <a href="https://github.com/sanskarpan/raft-consensus">Raft</a>
          implementation, a distributed tracing backend, an
          <a href="https://github.com/sanskarpan/promptline">LLM-evaluation pipeline</a>,
          and an agent-orchestration runtime, mostly in Go and Python. Reading gives you
          the vocabulary; building gives you the intuition.
        </p>

        <p>
          I care about first-principles understanding, evergreen writing over hot takes,
          and building things that hold up. This site is where I keep the notes:
          <a href="/writing">long-form writing</a>, the
          <a href="/projects">things I&rsquo;ve built</a>, and
          <a href="/notes">rougher notes</a> in the margins.
        </p>

        <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/sanskarpan">GitHub</a>, the source of most of the above</li>
          <li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/sanskarpandey2004">LinkedIn</a></li>
          <li><a href="mailto:sanskar.works.2004@gmail.com">Email</a>, the best way to reach me</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.9rem;">
          Want the short version? <a href="/uses">What I use</a> &middot; <a href="/now">what I&rsquo;m doing now</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
